Implementation of rename: read the old file, parse the fields, rewrite the content
 with the new id/title, write to the new file, and delete the old file. Note: load
_all reads all files in the directory, so the body may contain SEP, but splitn(4,
 SEP) handles that.

Edge case: if old_id == new_id, just rewrite the file. Implementation:

```rust
pub fn rename(dir: &Path, old_id: &str, new_id: &str, new_title: &str) -> std::io
::Result<()> {
    let old_path = dir.join(format!("{}.note", old_id));
    let content = fs::read_to_string(&old_path)?;
    let parts: Vec<&str> = content.splitn(4, SEP).collect();
    if parts.len() != 4 {
        return Err(std::io::Error::new(
            std::io::ErrorKind::InvalidData,
            "note file is malformed",
        ));
    }
    let pinned_flag = if parts[2] == "1" { "1" } else { "0" };
    let new_content = format!(
        "{}{}{}{}{}{}{}",
        new_id, SEP, new_title, SEP, pinned_flag, SEP, parts[3]
    );
    let new_path = dir.join(format!("{}.note", new_id));
    if old_path != new_path {
        fs::write(&new_path, new_content)?;
        fs::remove_file(&old_path)?;
    } else {
        fs::write(&new_path, new_content)?;
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

Note: `pinned_flag` — parts[2] is "0" or "1". Preserve the original value as-is.

